# Private TesseraBX add-ons to vendor into the build.
#
# The runner clones each repo below (using the prod host's git credentials)
# into the upstream tree's modules/<slug>/ BEFORE the docker build. The
# upstream Dockerfile then COPYs them into the image. Use this for PRIVATE
# add-ons, which cannot be installed from inside the docker build because
# the build has no git credentials. PUBLIC / ForgeBox add-ons go in
# overlay/box.addons.json instead.
#
# One add-on per line, whitespace-separated:
#
#   <git-url>                                          <ref>   <slug>
#
#   <git-url>  required. SSH form recommended for private repos.
#   <ref>      optional, default main. A branch, tag, or commit SHA.
#   <slug>     optional, default the repo name. Becomes modules/<slug>/.
#
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#
# EXAMPLE (this is a real private add-on; replace or remove it for your own
# deployment). Pin <ref> to a tag for reproducible production deploys:
git@github.com:oistechnologies/tesserabx-pm.git   main   tesserabx-pm
